      "narrative": "The copper lamps cast a dim, watery light across the scarred tabletop as you lean toward Mara Venn. Her charcoal coat rustles when she shifts, sharp eyes fixing on you with the patient stillness of someone used to being questioned.\n\nShe opens her mouth to answer\u2014but something across the room snags her attention. Her gaze flicks past your shoulder, narrows.\n\nYou follow her look. Toran Vex, the ink-stained clerk at the next table, has gone rigid, his cup frozen halfway to his lips, a sheen of sweat on his brow. He's staring at the two of you with undisguised alarm.\n\nMara's attention snaps back to you, and whatever thread she was about to pull is gone. She blinks, shakes her head slightly.\n\n\"Sorry,\" she says, and her voice has gone flatter. \"I don't know what you're after. The gate's shut. Bram's dead. That's all there is to it.\" She picks up her cup, takes a long drink, and doesn't meet your eyes.\n\nToran Vex sets his cup down with a *click* that rings too loud in the quiet tavern. He's already rising, fishing a few copper coins from his purse and dropping them on the table\u2014a man who's decided he's done with this room."
    },
