      "narrative": "Mara Venn's cup stops halfway to her lips. She sets it down slowly, and for a moment the only sound is rain drumming against the shuttered windows.\n\n\"Funny you should ask that.\" She tilts her head, studying you with new interest. \"The gate's lock was maintained by a locksmith. Name of Grom. Local man, works out of a little shop near the south market. He's the one who kept the mechanism turning smooth for years\u2014until someone filed the pins down to nothing.\"\n\nShe leans forward, elbows on the scarred wood. \"Grom's still in town, far as I know. If anyone can tell you what state that lock was in before it got ruined, it'd be him.\"\n\nAcross the room, Toran Vex has frozen mid-step, one hand still hovering over the coins he dropped. At the mention of Grom's name, he gives a short, jerky nod\u2014nervous confirmation.\n\nThen he ducks his head, pulls his collar up, and makes for the door."
    },
