      "narrative": "Mara Venn's eyes narrow at the insistence in your voice. She leans back, fingers drumming once against her cup.\n\n\"I told you,\" she says, each word measured, \"I don't know what you're after. The gate's shut. Bram's dead. That's the beginning and end of it.\"\n\nShe holds your gaze a beat too long, then looks away toward the rain-streaked window. Her jaw works like she's chewing on something she won't spit out.\n\n*She knows a name.* You can feel it hanging in the air between you\u2014a word she's decided not to speak. The way her thumb traces the rim of her cup, the slight tension in her shoulders. She's holding something back, and she's not going to give it up to pressing questions alone.\n\nThe tavern creaks around you. Rain drums. Mara Venn takes a slow sip of her drink and says nothing more.\n\nThrough the window, a figure in a travel-stained cloak crosses the muddy street toward the Ash Gate."
